<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/</link><lastBuildDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:28:01 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>West Bank: ‘Without international trade and financial support, large settlements would not exist’</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261113-west-bank-without-international-trade-and-financial-support-large-settlements-would-not-exist-1</link><description>
France is considering legislation to restrict trade with Israeli settlements in the occupied Palestinian territories, namely the West Bank. Ivar Ekeland, Professor Emeritus at Paris Dauphine-PSL University and Chair of the Organization of Academics for the Respect of International Law in Palestine, discusses the proposed measures with Alison Sargent. He calls for restrictions to cover n ot only goods but also services, including financial services, insurance and tourism. "Without the support of financial entities, of insurance, of providing goods and so on, settlements, big settlements, would not exist," he argues.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7d3f7e80-df7b-11f1-aba2-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261113-080847-081941-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7d3f7e80-df7b-11f1-aba2-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261113-080847-081941-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8270b5ae-df7b-11f1-9261-bb9885e86514</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:15:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>UN refugee chief Barham Salih slams 'shameful' war in Sudan, urges 'political solution'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261113-un-refugee-chief-barham-salih-slams-shameful-war-in-sudan-urges-political-solution</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24, UN refugee chief Barham Salih called the war in Sudan "shameful" and urged the world to end it. With forced displacement at a record high, he warned that funding cuts are hurting people "in dire need". "Efficiency has its limits," he said. Salih also defended the "integrity of the asylum system".
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/02c9f834-dea3-11f1-84f2-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/TaT-BARHAM-SALIH-pour-mix-V2-MIX-OK.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/02c9f834-dea3-11f1-84f2-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/TaT-BARHAM-SALIH-pour-mix-V2-MIX-OK.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">37a844bc-dea7-11f1-8b75-1591d7fd5df4</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:56:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Reporters</category><title>The truth about Douma: How Syria covered up a chemical attack</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20261113-the-truth-about-douma-how-syria-covered-up-a-chemical-attack</link><description>
On April 7, 2018, the Syrian town of Douma, on the outskirts of the capital Damascus, was targeted by a chemical attack. Evidence pointed to the Syrian regime, yet proof vanished, and eyewitnesses went silent. Eight years later, FRANCE 24's Jenna Le Bras tracked down survivors and witnesses of the deadly attack. She also met representatives of some of the world's most powerful institutions to understand how a massive cover-up campaign had been orchestrated by the regime, with Russian support.   
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6393738e-df57-11f1-9809-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/vignette-douma-mensonge-d-etat-EN-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6393738e-df57-11f1-9809-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/vignette-douma-mensonge-d-etat-EN-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">94e4bbda-df68-11f1-bace-abe937de67c9</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:24:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Jenna LE BRAS</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>'No war, no peace' situation between US and Iran 'cannot continue', Iraqi FM says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261113-no-war-and-no-peace-between-the-us-and-iran-cannot-continue-iraqi-fm-says</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24, Iraqi Foreign Minister Fuad Hussein said the "no war and no peace" situation in the region "cannot continue". He also said that closing all but two border crossings with Iran, as Washington demands, was "not possible". Finally, he confirmed that Iraqi oil now is now flowing through the Strait of Hormuz under US protection.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/36d19004-de87-11f1-be18-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/TETE-A-TETE-HUSSEIN-FOUAD-MIX-OK.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/36d19004-de87-11f1-be18-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/TETE-A-TETE-HUSSEIN-FOUAD-MIX-OK.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ddff67ee-de81-11f1-a151-6b48e96878ad</guid><pubDate>Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:28:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israeli strike on Gaza hospital kills six, including surgeon, medics say</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israeli-strike-on-gaza-hospital-kills-six-including-surgeon-medics-say</link><description>
Israeli fire killed 11 people in Gaza on Thursday, six of them in the bombing of Nasser hospital in south Gaza early in the day, health officials said, the deadliest single strike since Israel's elections last month. FRANCE 24's Mark Owen speaks with Dr Goher Rahbour, a surgeon working at the Nasser Hospital.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d8bb4c84-ded2-11f1-b9be-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261112-203639-204648-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d8bb4c84-ded2-11f1-b9be-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261112-203639-204648-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ddeb127a-ded2-11f1-aba1-f38243617a56</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:03:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel to ban far-left French politician Jean-Luc Mélenchon from entry</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261112-israel-to-ban-far-left-french-politician-jean-luc-m%C3%A9lenchon-from-entry</link><description>
The Israeli government said Thursday that it would ban far-left French leader Jean-Luc Mélenchon from entering the country after the French presidential contender said he would use French vessels to force aid into Gaza if he were elected. The announcement comes a day after France confirmed it had refused entry to the head of a body representing settlements in the occupied West Bank.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33654616-dab0-11f1-ad25-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-14T100614Z-1152484815-RC2Y2OATJ5N2-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-POLITICS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33654616-dab0-11f1-ad25-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-14T100614Z-1152484815-RC2Y2OATJ5N2-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-POLITICS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8866be1e-debc-11f1-bc46-a78d57209718</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:43:03 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/33654616-dab0-11f1-ad25-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-14T100614Z-1152484815-RC2Y2OATJ5N2-RTRMADP-3-FRANCE-POLITICS.jpg">© Abdul Saboor, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel kills six in Gaza hospital strike as 9-month-old baby freezes to death</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261112-israel-kills-six-in-gaza-hospital-strike-as-9-month-old-baby-freezes-to-death</link><description>
An overnight Israeli air strike on Nasser Hospital in southern Gaza killed at least six Palestinians Thursday, including a teenage boy and a surgeon, medics said. Elsewhere in the devastated Palestinian territory, a nine-month-old baby died from the cold as families flee worsening flooding.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2915f31c-dead-11f1-ba4a-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-12T043325Z-1772503551-RC23MOA2UKYO-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-GAZA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2915f31c-dead-11f1-ba4a-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-12T043325Z-1772503551-RC23MOA2UKYO-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-GAZA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bb02b8d8-deac-11f1-8b1d-e74430e79b3b</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:18:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/2915f31c-dead-11f1-ba4a-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-12T043325Z-1772503551-RC23MOA2UKYO-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-PALESTINIANS-GAZA.jpg">© Ramadan Abed, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>How FRANCE 24 traced Tehran-backed Afghan fighters from Syria to southeastern Iran</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261112-iran-afghan-fatemiyoun-fighters-syria-baluchistan</link><description>
Members of the Tehran-backed Afghan Shia militia known as the Fatemiyoun division have resurfaced in Iran after largely disappearing from public view following the fall of Bashar al-Assad’s government in Syria in 2024. FRANCE 24 used "martyrdom” announcements and the geolocation of videos shared on social media to trace their presence. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84498144-dea4-11f1-ad4b-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/fat-main-photo.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84498144-dea4-11f1-ad4b-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/fat-main-photo.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0d6127e6-dea7-11f1-884f-3be5653ca07f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:03:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84498144-dea4-11f1-ad4b-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/fat-main-photo.jpg">© Observers</source><dc:creator>Ershad ALIJANI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Israeli occupation in southern Lebanon: Displaced families struggle to cope</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261112-israeli-occupation-in-southern-lebanon-displaced-families-struggle-to-cope</link><description>
In Lebanon, more than 360,000 people are still displaced after months of war between Israel and Hezbollah, according to the UN. Along the border, the Israeli army claims to be fighting the Iran-backed militant group but now occupies 6 percent of Lebanese territory and is wiping entire villages off the map. In the border area, we meet families living in makeshift housing. Many fear they may never go home.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/38e48628-ddf9-11f1-82b6-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-FREEZE-LEBANON-ISRAELI-OCCUPATION-BAIN-Lauren-Sub.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/38e48628-ddf9-11f1-82b6-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-NW-OOV-FREEZE-LEBANON-ISRAELI-OCCUPATION-BAIN-Lauren-Sub.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d7e34142-ddf9-11f1-ba1f-d72171b1cb65</guid><pubDate>Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:51:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Sophie GUIGNON</dc:creator></item><item><category>A propos</category><title>Gadi Eisenkot unveils agenda to reverse Netanyahu’s policies</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20261111-gadi-eisenkot-unveils-agenda-to-reverse-netanyahu-s-policies</link><description>
The bloc of Israeli prime ministerial hopeful Gadi Eisenkot introduced a series of bills at the start of the legislative session that target Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and his policies. They include launching an official government-led inquiry into the Hamas-led October 7, 2023 attacks, setting term limits on the position of prime minister and overturning changes the outgoing Netanyahu-led government made to limit the powers of the judiciary. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Rina Bassist, Editor at Al-Monitor.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8b2b3982-de7a-11f1-9d73-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-f44ef0f1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8b2b3982-de7a-11f1-9d73-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-f44ef0f1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">122ae710-de1d-11f1-aaa4-c1c2bf00e785</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:13:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Sharon GAFFNEY</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Gadi Eisenkot unveils agenda to reverse Netanyahu’s policies</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/gadi-eisenkot-unveils-agenda-to-reverse-netanyahu-s-policies</link><description>
The bloc of Israeli prime ministerial hopeful Gadi Eisenkot introduced a series of bills at the start of the legislative session that target Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and his policies. They include launching an official government-led inquiry into the Hamas-led October 7, 2023 attacks, setting term limits on the position of prime minister and overturning changes the outgoing Netanyahu-led government made to limit the powers of the judiciary. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Rina Bassist, Editor at Al-Monitor.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8b2b3982-de7a-11f1-9d73-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-f44ef0f1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8b2b3982-de7a-11f1-9d73-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-f44ef0f1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cf1f26bc-de1b-11f1-828e-f1fb8133ff5f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 22:11:46 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Eisenkot quickly targets Netanyahu's legacy in new Israeli parliament</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/eisenkot-quickly-targets-netanyahu-s-legacy-in-new-israeli-parliament</link><description>
Israeli ex-army chief Gadi Eisenkot and his allies launched a legislative onslaught against caretaker Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's legacy on Tuesday, as a new parliament convened in a heated first session.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8491a9b4-ddb0-11f1-897d-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261111-080849-081212-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8491a9b4-ddb0-11f1-897d-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261111-080849-081212-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">895e049c-ddb0-11f1-a157-7b99786cc99c</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:29:28 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Egyptian journalist Lina Attalah faces prison as trial sparks international outcry</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261111-lina-attalah-egypt-trial-prison</link><description>
Egyptian journalist Lina Attalah, head of independent news outlet Mada Masr, faces a criminal court retrial Wednesday over charges of operating without a licence and publishing false news. The UN criticised Egypt’s “widening assaults on press freedom” Tuesday. Attalah was previously handed a one-year prison sentence in absentia in 2024.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f471bf6c-dd6f-11f1-b88a-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/a44f4102d9b1178ba8efb41cfeca20fa077097ab.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f471bf6c-dd6f-11f1-b88a-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/a44f4102d9b1178ba8efb41cfeca20fa077097ab.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b28f2c5e-dd71-11f1-9beb-d78b5b97da2a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 11 Nov 2026 01:53:51 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f471bf6c-dd6f-11f1-b88a-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/a44f4102d9b1178ba8efb41cfeca20fa077097ab.jpg">© Khaled Desouki, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Eisenkot pushes October 7 inquiry as Netanyahu targets Arab parties in tense new parliament</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261110-eisenkot-pushes-october-7-inquiry-as-netanyahu-targets-arab-parties-in-tense-new-parliament</link><description>
Gadi Eisenkot, the politician tasked with forming a new Israeli government, pledged on Tuesday to launch an official inquiry into Hamas's October 7, 2023 attacks and reverse many of Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's policies as the new parliament was sworn in a tense opening session that saw rival parties trade barbs over the possibility of forming a government with the support of Arab lists.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c3264e3e-dd4f-11f1-a6a1-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26314586138425.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c3264e3e-dd4f-11f1-a6a1-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26314586138425.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e4b03f38-dd4f-11f1-8261-3ba878fe5186</guid><pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:53:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c3264e3e-dd4f-11f1-a6a1-3f371022a770/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26314586138425.jpg">© Ohad Zwigenberg, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Asymmetric cyberwarfare: 'States increasingly use cyberattacks in support of their other objectives'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asymmetric-cyberwarfare-states-increasingly-use-cyberattacks-in-support-of-their-other-objectives</link><description>
Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Rafe Pilling, Director of Threat Intelligence in the Sophos Counter Threat Unit (CTU). How can a minor cyber intrusion disrupt food supplies, expose the weaknesses of industrial infrastructure and become an instrument of geopolitical confrontation? The cyberattacks targeting supermarket refrigeration systems in France offer a revealing illustration of how digital vulnerabilities can translate into tangible economic disruption and potentially broader threats to society. As Pilling explains, “With a small amount of effort from the adversary side, they can create a large impact, in this case destroying food and producing empty shelves or empty refrigeration units in stores.” This asymmetry lies at the heart of contemporary cyber conflict, in which modest technical interventions can produce disproportionate economic and operational consequences
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54ae7cc8-dd4b-11f1-a4f5-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261110-150753-151904-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54ae7cc8-dd4b-11f1-a4f5-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261110-150753-151904-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5a443a88-dd4b-11f1-adec-d3e0d8281655</guid><pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:25:45 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Netanyahu bloc targets Arab lawmakers as Israel's new parliament is sworn in</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261110-live-new-israeli-parliament-sworn-in-eisenkot-aims-to-form-government-netanyahu-knesset</link><description>
Tensions ran high at the first session of Israel's new parliament on Tuesday as rival camps traded barbs over the possibility of ruling with the support of Arab lists. The party of opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot, who has been tasked with forming a government, moved to immediately set up a commission to investigate Hamas's October 7, 2023 attack, an action long resisted by Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. Read our blog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c42ebe6a-dd1d-11f1-b173-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-10T143111Z-351398299-RC22LOATL231-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-POLITICS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c42ebe6a-dd1d-11f1-b173-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-10T143111Z-351398299-RC22LOATL231-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-POLITICS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">279e7fcc-dd13-11f1-994d-05cf1ea115bd</guid><pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 14:40:16 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c42ebe6a-dd1d-11f1-b173-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-10T143111Z-351398299-RC22LOATL231-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-POLITICS.jpg">© Ronen Zvulun, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>New Israel parliament to be sworn in as Eisenkot works to form new govt</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261110-new-israel-parliament-to-be-sworn-in-as-eisenkot-works-to-form-new-govt</link><description>
Israel's new parliament will be sworn on Tuesday, November 10, with Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu set to lose his majority as rival Gadi Eisenkot works to form a new government. The opposition hopes to use its newfound legislative power to move quickly on key priorities, including a commission to investigate security failures under Netanyahu that allowed the October 7, 2023 attack by Hamas. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Jerusalem Noga Tarnopolsky has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ca01015e-dcf5-11f1-bb13-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a1c9673b.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ca01015e-dcf5-11f1-bb13-29048b396e03/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-a1c9673b.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f9ad13ee-dcf4-11f1-b6f4-333395c1bad3</guid><pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:22:39 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel's new parliament to be sworn in as Eisenkot prepares government</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261110-israel-s-new-parliament-to-be-sworn-in-as-eisenkot-forms-government</link><description>
Israel's new parliament is set to be sworn in Tuesday with neither Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's bloc nor opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot's camp holding a majority. Eisenkot seeks to build a coalition after receiving a mandate to form a government.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0f59d90-dcac-11f1-a153-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/9b610a941f6ae20f37bc1c1b99b4ec1e444a97c1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0f59d90-dcac-11f1-a153-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/9b610a941f6ae20f37bc1c1b99b4ec1e444a97c1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9e325d56-dce7-11f1-a84a-a917def10fd8</guid><pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 09:17:56 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f0f59d90-dcac-11f1-a153-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/9b610a941f6ae20f37bc1c1b99b4ec1e444a97c1.jpg">© Ilia Yefimovich, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Will Eisenkot succeed in 'minefield of Israeli politics' where 'so many other generals' have failed?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261109-will-eisenkot-succeed-in-minefield-of-israeli-politics-where-so-many-other-generals-have-failed</link><description>
François Picard welcomes Dahlia Scheindlin, Israeli political analyst, strategic consultant and pollster, to examine a question that reaches far beyond the immediate struggle for power: Can Israel move beyond PM Benjamin Netanyahu amid coalition deadlock, growing disillusionment in Washington and the persistent limits of political inclusion?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0c76a7fe-dd0b-11f1-b950-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-53f97b5e.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/0c76a7fe-dd0b-11f1-b950-5f54d898a954/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-53f97b5e.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a36f2ff2-dc78-11f1-b354-2967f119a46a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 20:03:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>'We think' the Iranians and Americans want to negotiate, Egyptian FM says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261109-we-think-the-iranians-and-americans-want-to-negotiate-egyptian-fm-says</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24, Egyptian Foreign Minister Badr Abdelatty said he believed Iran and the United States wanted to negotiate, but called for a "concrete deal" to prevent another escalation. He also said Cairo was still "counting" on US President Donald Trump to "move forward" with the stalled Gaza peace plan and was "confident" US military aid to Egypt would continue. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b7f4021e-dc3b-11f1-a48b-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/MAE-EGYPTIEN-PLAN-INVITE-2026-11-09-F24.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b7f4021e-dc3b-11f1-a48b-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/MAE-EGYPTIEN-PLAN-INVITE-2026-11-09-F24.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">71874660-dc27-11f1-b46c-fbffa696f57a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 19:31:42 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Life in Gaza simply miserable': Amid flooding, lack of aid, conditions 'worsen' for Palestinians</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/life-in-gaza-simply-miserable-amid-flooding-lack-of-aid-conditions-worsen-for-palestinians</link><description>
Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Shaina Low, Communication Adviser for the Norwegian Refugee Council (NRC). Thirteen months into what she describes as a "so-called ceasefire," the humanitarian crisis in Gaza continues to deepen, exposing the profound gap between diplomatic commitments and the lived realities of Palestinian civilians. In an interview with France 24, Shayna Low, communications adviser in Palestine for the Norwegian Refugee Council (NRC), describes a population confronting winter flooding, repeated displacement, deteriorating shelter conditions and persistent restrictions on humanitarian assistance. "Life in Gaza is simply miserable." Low urges Israel to "open all the crossings, lift the restrictions, let aid in."
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e3d3edca-dc60-11f1-8648-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261109-160607-161526-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/e3d3edca-dc60-11f1-8648-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261109-160607-161526-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e94ce432-dc60-11f1-96d5-cb6fc6fe985c</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 17:26:51 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Perspective</category><title>Iran 'has mistaken perception' of US midterm result, expert says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/iran-sees-golden-opportunity-for-a-sweetheart-deal-after-us-midterms-expert-says</link><description>
A leading commentator on Iran says the country sees the results of the US midterm elections as giving them a golden opportunity for a sweet deal. Paymon Azmoudeh from Forward Global was speaking amid conflicting statements from the key players about whether there will be further US military action in Iran. President Donald Trump says that renewed strikes on Iran are "highly unlikely" if talks progress. However, Iran's foreign minister says the midterms have brought a ⁠pause to mediators' work. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bf8bded8-dc41-11f1-bc20-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d352b274.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bf8bded8-dc41-11f1-bc20-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-d352b274.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">840f214c-dc20-11f1-8b82-83ba838a7e78</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 13:49:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Stuart NORVAL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Saudi Arabia intercepts Houthi missiles as Riyadh's Aramco building damaged</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-saudi-arabia-intercepts-houthi-missiles-as-riyadh-s-aramco-building-damaged</link><description>
Saudi Arabia intercepted incoming missiles from Yemen's Houthi rebels targeting the kingdom's capital and other regions on Sunday, November 8, with falling debris damaging a building belonging to the state-owned oil giant Aramco in Riyadh’s financial district. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/24a0a774-dc27-11f1-ad5f-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6369a9a0.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/24a0a774-dc27-11f1-ad5f-1beafce15fea/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-6369a9a0.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d95bd950-dc26-11f1-bf73-a7a7016cb462</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 10:41:55 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel's opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot has six weeks to form a government</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261109-israel-s-opposition-leader-gadi-eisenkot-has-six-weeks-to-form-a-government</link><description>
Israeli President Isaac Herzog formally gave opposition politician Gadi Eisenkot the first chance to form the next government Sunday evening, leaving Eisenkot six weeks to try to put together a coalition to oust Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu. FRANCE 24's correspondent in Jerusalem Noga Tarnopolsky has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cbef71e4-dc23-11f1-882d-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-f52ea606.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cbef71e4-dc23-11f1-882d-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-f52ea606.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">396313d0-dc23-11f1-9ef6-d590fdfa7516</guid><pubDate>Mon, 09 Nov 2026 10:36:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israeli opposition leader Eisenkot begins the hard work of forging a coalition government</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261108-israeli-opposition-leader-eisenkot-begins-the-hard-work-of-forging-a-coalition-government</link><description>
Israel's ex-military chief Gadi Eisenkot was tapped by President Isaac Herzog to try to form a government Sunday evening. But his lack of a clear majority in parliament will make trying to forge a coalition alongside the country's divided minor parties an uphill struggle.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be4c1c22-dbb5-11f1-bbd7-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-08T152158Z-1569314181-RC2RJOASDUSW-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-POLITICS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be4c1c22-dbb5-11f1-bbd7-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-08T152158Z-1569314181-RC2RJOASDUSW-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-POLITICS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">369dc2a8-dbb5-11f1-8464-4d6ebdc8c05c</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 21:10:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/be4c1c22-dbb5-11f1-bbd7-a575454bc579/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-08T152158Z-1569314181-RC2RJOASDUSW-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-POLITICS.jpg">© Ronen Zvulun, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Gadi Eisenkot receives mandate to form government</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/gadi-eisenkot-receives-mandate-to-form-government</link><description>
Israel's opposition leader Gadi Eisenkot has officially been tasked with forming the country's next government, following a formal announcement by President Isaac Herzog. He now has up to six weeks to negotiate with potential coalition partners and secure a parliamentary majority. While an alliance with Arab Israeli parties appears to be the easiest option mathematically, it remains politically sensitive. Eisenkot must now navigate difficult negotiations to build a coalition capable of replacing Benjamin Netanyahu. Noga Tarnopolsky reports from Jerusalem.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/608ffe0e-db93-11f1-85ef-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-160801-161121-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/608ffe0e-db93-11f1-85ef-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-160801-161121-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">65b815e2-db93-11f1-9ee7-4943b8d2bb10</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 16:58:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Yemen's humanitarian crisis worsens</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-s-humanitarian-crisis-worsens</link><description>
One month into the Yemeni government's offensive against the Iran-aligned Houthis, fighting continues to escalate along the Red Sea coast. Meanwhile, the humanitarian crisis is worsening, with hundreds of thousands of people displaced and the country facing the threat of catastrophe. Rula Amin, Senior Communications Advisor and spokesperson at UNHCR at Amman, in Jordan, shares further details.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61e95800-db7e-11f1-961e-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-140416-140658-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61e95800-db7e-11f1-961e-d18c5759e759/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-140416-140658-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6735dcac-db7e-11f1-b6b0-a3bc1c7deeec</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 14:22:14 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israeli president officially tasks Eisenkot with forming government</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261108-middle-east-live-riyadh-financial-district-targeted-deadly-strikes-yemen-israel-eisenkot-netanyahu-coalition-government-elections</link><description>
Israeli President Isaac Herzog on Sunday officially tasked ex-military chief Gadi Eisenkot with trying to form a government after neither Eisenkot's bloc nor that or incumbent Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu won a clear majority in Israel's October 27 elections. Eisenkot now has up to six weeks to form a coalition government. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f71c892a-db87-11f1-9c18-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-08T151738Z-84214136-RC2RJOAONV9B-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-POLITICS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f71c892a-db87-11f1-9c18-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-08T151738Z-84214136-RC2RJOAONV9B-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-POLITICS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4f9136bc-db58-11f1-b6e9-1d122f9c1034</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 09:47:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f71c892a-db87-11f1-9c18-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-11-08T151738Z-84214136-RC2RJOAONV9B-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-POLITICS.jpg">© Ronen Zvulun, Reuters</source><dc:creator>Louise NORDSTROM</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel's Arab-led parties gain influence</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israel-s-arab-led-parties-gain-influence</link><description>
Arab-led parties have endorsed Gadi Eisenkot despite his ruling out a coalition with them. Their support is driven by a shared goal: removing Benjamin Netanyahu from power. But could these parties ultimately hold the balance of power in forming Israel's next government? Antonia Kerrigan reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dec0c3da-db57-11f1-b79b-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-100714-100924-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/dec0c3da-db57-11f1-b79b-bf1914cabd52/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-100714-100924-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e3c19d0a-db57-11f1-afce-7d507642ff15</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 09:43:26 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Gaza: Heavy rain inundates thousands of tents</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/gaza-heavy-rain-inundates-thousands-of-tents</link><description>
Heavy rainfall has flooded thousands of tents sheltering displaced Palestinians across the Gaza Strip, including in Deir al-Balah. Residents say overflowing sewage has mixed with the floodwater, further worsening already dire living conditions. Families are struggling to salvage their belongings, building makeshift earthen barriers and trying to drain the water by hand. Many have seen essential items soaked and rendered unusable, adding to the hardship faced by those already displaced.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25796fa2-db58-11f1-946f-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-100942-101123-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25796fa2-db58-11f1-946f-695cb59fade5/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261108-100942-101123-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2ac0b998-db58-11f1-a8f1-2946bdd1dc7c</guid><pubDate>Sun, 08 Nov 2026 09:42:03 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item></channel></rss>
